Ether (ETH) is Ethereum's currency, and its smallest unit is wei (1 ETH = 10¹⁸ wei).
Wallets like MetaMask, Rabby, and Phantom help users manage Ethereum accounts and sign transactions.
Users should control their own private keys and securely back up their 12-word seed phrase, preferably on paper. Losing it means losing access to funds permanently.
MetaMask can connect to different networks, including Ethereum Mainnet, Sepolia, and Holesky testnets.
Test ETH can be obtained from Sepolia faucets to practice without risking real money.
Every Ethereum transaction requires gas fees, paid in ETH, even on test networks.
Ethereum is more than a cryptocurrency; it is a decentralized world computer powered by the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM).
There are two types of accounts:
EOAs (Externally Owned Accounts): controlled by private keys.
Contract Accounts: controlled by smart contract code.
